    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47925": {
      "title": "Transcript Specialist II",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Transcript Specialist II Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Transcript Specialist II Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF2560P Position Title Transcript Specialist II Position Type Classified Staff/Hourly Department Records Office - Global - Troy Division Finance and Administration Campus Troy Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Transcript Specialist II position is responsible for but not limited to: Processing and issuing transcript requests both electronically and paper, including mail orders from other institutions, individual students and through Parchment. Answering incoming calls to the department, assisting with transcript inquiries for current and former students, assists with ordering transcripts, and process for ordering unofficial transcripts, determining if transcripts have been received from other schools, answering all general questions regarding transcripts; assisting special investigators, employers, and other colleges with transcript inquiries, background checks, degree verifications, etc. Managing departmental email, including processing and issuing transcripts, corresponding with other departments to assist in distribution of information in regards to transcripts. Retrieve records from the vault and scan into document Imaging, scanning for Admissions as requested. Issue course descriptions as requested File records in vault after completion of document imaging process Assist walk-in student’s with requests for transcripts, general questions, etc. Other duties as required by supervisor Minimum Qualifications 1. High school diploma or equivalent 2. Excellent computer skills 3. Excellent interpersonal, written and verbal skills 4. Positive attitude 5. Attention to detail 6. Ability to multi-task 7. Working knowledge of Microsoft Operating Systems and Windows Office Preferred Qualifications 1. Bachelor’s degree in a related field 2. Experience in a higher education environment 3. Experience in student services 4. Knowledge of Datatel student management system Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? No Work Hours Monday – Friday 8 am – 5 pm List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position NA Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 07/22/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47909 Reference Letters Reference Letters Solicit References Through the System? No Last Day a Reference Provider Can Submit Reference Applicant Special Instructions Qualified applications will be made available to the department/committee for review immediately upon submission. We ask that you provide email addresses for your reference providers and please be certain that the email addresses you list are accurate. If you are selected as a candidate for consideration by the department/committee, an instructional email will be sent to your reference providers to ask that they submit a reference letter on your behalf via a link to our reference portal. Separate reference letters will be requested for each position to which you apply (if applicable), so your reference providers will be con