    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48395": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Payroll Services",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Assistant Director of Payroll Services Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Assistant Director of Payroll Services Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF2476P Position Title Assistant Director of Payroll Services Position Type Professional/Salaried Department Payroll Services - Troy Division Finance and Administration Campus Troy Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Assistant Director of Payroll Services position serves as a strategic partner in leading all payroll operations for the university. This role provides hands-on oversight of payroll processing, compliance, and system administration while supporting the Director of Payroll in developing policies, implementing improvements, and ensuring exceptional service delivery. The Assistant Director manages day-to-day operations, supervises payroll staff, and serves as a subject matter expert on complex payroll matters affecting faculty, staff, graduate assistants, and student employees. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or related field Minimum 5 years of progressive payroll experience, with at least 2 years in a lead or supervisory capacity Comprehensive knowledge of federal and state payroll tax laws, FLSA regulations, and wage and hour compliance Demonstrated proficiency with payroll systems Experience with general ledger reconciliation and accounting principles Strong supervisory skills with the ability to train, mentor, and evaluate staff Exceptional attention to detail and commitment to accuracy Excellent analytical and problem-solving abilities Strong written and verbal communication skills Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet strict deadlines Proficiency in Microsoft Excel and database reporting tools Preferred Qualifications Certified Payroll Professional ( CPP ) or Fundamental Payroll Certification ( FPC ) Higher education payroll experience with understanding of academic appointment types and faculty compensation structures Experience with state retirement systems, TRS , TIAA , or pension plan reporting Knowledge of grant and auxiliary fund accounting in a university environment Experience with Colleague, Banner, PeopleSoft, Workday, or similar enterprise systems Advanced Excel skills including pivot tables, VLOOKUP , and data analysis Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? Work Hours 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Monday – Friday List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position NA Does this position have supervisory responsibility? Yes Posting Date 09/03/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46706 Reference Letters Reference Letters Solicit References Through the System? No Last Day a Reference Provider Can Submit Reference Applicant Special Instructions Qualified applications will be made available to the department/committee for review immediately upon submission. We ask that you provide email addresses for your reference providers and please be certain that the email addresses you list are accurate. If you are selected as a candidate for consideration by the department/committee, 