    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48397": {
      "title": "Graduate Research Assistant",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Graduate Research Assistant - MSIR Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Graduate Research Assistant - MSIR Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number ST1400P Position Title Graduate Research Assistant - MSIR Position Type Student Department School of Social Sciences – Political Science - Troy Division College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Campus Troy Work Status Student (SPT) Temporary Yes Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Center for Eastern and Central European, Russian, and Eurasian Studies ( CECERES ) at Troy University seeks a highly motivated Graduate Research Assistant to support the research activities of the Center Director and affiliated faculty. This position is designed for graduate students with strong analytical and writing skills who are interested in academic research, policy analysis, and international affairs. The Graduate Research Assistant will contribute directly to faculty research projects, publications, grant proposals, and policy-oriented outputs related to Eastern and Central Europe, Russia, and Eurasia. About the Center: The Center for Eastern and Central European, Russian, and Eurasian Studies is an interdisciplinary research center focused on the politics, security, history, and societies of Eastern and Central Europe, Russia, and Eurasia. The Center supports faculty and student research, hosts scholarly and public events, and contributes to policy-relevant debates through research dissemination and external engagement. Key Responsibilities: Conduct literature reviews and background research for faculty and Director-led projects. Assist with data collection and organization, including qualitative and quantitative sources. Support drafting and editing of academic manuscripts, policy briefs, reports, and grant applications. Track developments related to regional politics, security, and international affairs. Compile annotated bibliographies and research memorandum. Assist with preparation of presentations, conference materials, and research summaries. Support collaborative research projects involving multiple faculty members. Minimum Qualifications Must be a currently enrolled Master of International Relations graduate student in good standing at Troy University . Strong research, writing, and analytical skills. Ability to synthesize complex academic and policy material clearly and accurately. Demonstrated interest in international relations, political science, area studies, or a related field. High level of professionalism, discretion, and reliability. Preferred Qualifications Coursework or background in Eastern European, Russian, or Eurasian studies. Experience with academic databases (e.g., JSTOR , Scopus, Web of Science). Foreign language skills relevant to the region (e.g., Russian or other regional languages). Experience with citation management software (e.g., Zotero, EndNote). Prior experience assisting faculty research or contributing to academic publications. Professional Development Opportunities: This position offers close mentorship with faculty, exposure to advanced research methods, and the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to publications and policy-relevant research. It is particularly well suited for students considering doctoral study, research careers, or work in policy and analytical institutions. Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? No Work Hours Maximum of 20 hours per week List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 09/03/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46640 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Do you currently work in another position for Troy University? No Yes - if hired for this position, intend to resign from other position Yes - if hired for this position, intend to keep other position * Are you a current Troy University graduate student, or will you be a graduate student at the start of employment? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Unofficial Transcript  1 Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Unofficial Transcript  2 - Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. - Troy University is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. - Troy University participates in eVerify. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
