    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47023": {
      "title": "Workship",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Workship - Civic Life Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Workship - Civic Life Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number ST1412P Position Title Workship - Civic Life Position Type Student Department Civic Engagement - Troy Division Academic Affairs Campus Troy Work Status Student (SPT) Temporary Yes Location Troy - T01 Job Summary This student worker position is responsible for leading the Civic Lab, supporting student engagement by connecting learning to real community needs through hands-on programming and partnerships, including a collaboration with the David Mathews Center for Civic Life. This role assists in planning and facilitating workshops and discussions for college students, while also working directly with youth in local schools to deliver activities related to civic responsibility and community involvement. Responsibilities include coordinating and leading volunteers, organizing events, supporting outreach efforts, and helping plan and implement initiatives such as a summer civics camp for elementary students. The position also involves collaborating with campus and community partners and assisting with basic program tracking and evaluation. This role also contributes to broader Office of Civic Engagement initiatives, helping connect students with meaningful opportunities to serve and engage in the community. Minimum Qualifications Must be a current Troy University student enrolled at least half-time. Interest in civic engagement, community service, and local community issues Ability to work independently and as part of a team Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage effectively with both campus and community stakeholders Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Demonstrated leadership experience through campus involvement, work, or other activities Prior volunteer experience Please note: Student positions are FICA /Medicare exempt only if students are enrolled in classes in the semester work is performed. To qualify for the FICA /Medicare exemption, you must be enrolled on a half-time basis for the Fall, Spring, or Summer. Preferred Qualifications Experience leading or coordinating volunteers Experience planning or organizing events, programs, or activities Experience working with youth or in school settings Experience facilitating or supporting group discussions in a respectful and engaging manner Creativity and willingness to contribute ideas for programming and engagement Additional leadership, communication, or community engagement experience beyond the required qualifications Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? No Work Hours 15 hours per week List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position Ability to lift and/or move up to 25 lbs Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 04/17/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Position is funded by external sponsor agency. Troy University is under no obligation to maintain this position if funding from external source is reduced or ceased. Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47019 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Are you a current Troy University student enrolled at least half-time, or will you be enrolled at least half-time by the start of employment? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents - Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. - Troy University is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. - Troy University participates in eVerify. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47927": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1075P Position Title Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor Position Type Faculty Department Department of C R I T - Global Division College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Campus Troy Online Faculty Rank If Faculty position 12 Month Is this position tenure track or non-tenure track? Dependent on selected rank Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location eTroy Job Summary The Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor of Counseling, Rehabilitation and Interpreter Training position in the College of Education & Behavioral Sciences is primarily responsible for teaching specialized graduate courses in clinical mental health counseling and other counseling specialties; pursuit of a scholarship and research agenda; service on committees at all levels; involvement in service to the community; advising graduate students; and supervising Practicum and Internship students. In Class Teaching Percentage Online Teaching Percentage Minimum Qualifications 1. Earned doctorate in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP -accredited program by the date of appointment. 2. Professional identity as a counselor demonstrated through academic preparation, professional experience, and engagement in the counseling profession. 3. Eligibility for counselor licensure in Alabama (e.g., LPC or equivalent). 4. Academic preparation and/or professional experience in Clinical Mental Health Counseling, School Counseling, Rehabilitation Counseling, or a closely related counseling specialty. 5. Demonstrated ability to teach and mentor graduate counseling students in an online learning environment. Preferred Qualifications 1. Current professional counselor licensure ( LPC or equivalent). 2. Experience teaching in a CACREP -accredited counselor education program. 3. Experience supervising practicum and internship students consistent with CACREP standards. 4. Evidence of scholarship, research, grant activity, presentations, or publications in counseling or counselor education (required for tenure-track consideration). 5. Experience with online instruction, student retention initiatives, program assessment, and accreditation processes. Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? Driving may be necessary but is not a primary responsibility Work Hours Based on faculty class schedule and departmental needs. List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position NA Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 07/22/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Academic Term Position Will Begin Fall 2026 Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47905 Reference Letters Reference Letters Last Day a Reference Provider Can Submit Reference Applicant Special Instructions Qualified applications will be made available to the department/committee for review immediately upon submission. We ask that you provide email addresses for your reference providers and please be certain that the email addresses you list are accurate. If you are selected as a candidate for consideration by the department/committee, an instructional email will be sent to your reference providers to ask that they submit a reference letter on your behalf via a link to our reference portal. Separate reference letters will be requested for each position to which you apply (if applicable), so your reference providers will be contacted separately for each application on which you list them. Reference letters will not be copied from one application to another. You can assure your reference providers that our system is secure and that all letters are confidential. If your reference providers have trouble using the reference portal, please advise them to contact jobs@troy.edu. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Do you have an earned doctorate degree in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP-accredited program? Yes No * Do you have, or are you eligible for, counselor licensure in Alabama (e.g., LPC or equivalent)? Yes No * Do you have academic preparation and/or professional experience in Clinical Mental Health Counseling, School Counseling, Rehabilitation Counseling, or a closely related counseling specialty? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter List of References Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcript  1 Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Resume Letter of Reference 1 Unofficial Transcript  2 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Unofficial Transcript 3 Other Document - Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. - Troy University is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. - Troy University participates in eVerify. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
