      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Vision Rehabilitation Assistant Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Vision Rehabilitation Assistant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF2532P Position Title Vision Rehabilitation Assistant Position Type Classified Staff/Hourly Department Human Services - Troy Division College of Health Sciences Campus Troy Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location Troy - T01 Job Summary PLEASE NOTE : Position is located in Talladega, AL The Vision Rehabilitation Assistant position is responsible for: Interact with public so that ADRS is represented in a positive manner via phone or in person. Transport and accompany State Coordinator of Blind Services on a statewide basis including extensive overnight and occasional weekend travel. Complete travel forms, time sheets, and leave requests in a timely manner. Maintain Outlook Calendar. Inventory and monitor program supplies. Prepare and distribute handouts/reports. Read written correspondence for Coordinator of Blind Services. Order and organize supplies for special programs. Utilize computer and assistive technology to transcribe materials for State Coordinator of Blind Services and other staff in an accessible format (Braille, large print, and electronic). Perform other duties as assigned by State Coordinator of Blind Services. Minimum Qualifications 1. 