    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47776": {
      "title": "Workship",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Workship Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Workship Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number ST1293P Position Title Workship Position Type Student Department Civic Engagement - Troy Division Academic Affairs Campus Troy Work Status Student (SPT) Temporary Yes Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Workship position serves to implement programming in the Office of Civic Engagement. Student workers are responsible for communicating effectively with internal and external stakeholders; taking initiative to plan, organize and implement academic and co-curricular programming; multitasking and working in a fast-paced environment; assisting with administrative support; working with local youth and seniors; flexibility to change plans regularly to meet adapting needs; contributing to a positive environment for colleagues and volunteers; other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications 1. Must be a current Troy University student enrolled at least half-time. 2. Ability to perform work with a strong attention to detail 3. Proficient skill at Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint 4. Experience serving in community and non-profit contexts Please note: Student positions are FICA /Medicare exempt only if students are enrolled in classes in the semester work is performed. To qualify for the FICA /Medicare exemption, you must be enrolled on a half-time basis for the Fall, Spring, or Summer. Preferred Qualifications 1. Experience mentoring 2. Experience leading groups 3. Participation in service projects 4. Experience giving presentations 5. Experience managing social media 6. Participation in discussions on current events 7. Publicity Experience (designing flyers, social media post) 8. Office Experience (answering phones/emails, filing paperwork) 9. Experience working with community agencies (nonprofit, school, government agency, etc.) Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? Driving may be necessary but is not a primary responsibility Work Hours 15 hours per week List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 07/06/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/43853 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Are you a current Troy University student enrolled at least half-time, or will you be enrolled at least half-time by the start of employment? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Unofficial Transcript  1 - Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. - Troy University is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. - Troy University participates in eVerify. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
