    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47961": {
      "title": "Director of International Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Director of International Enrollment Management Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Director of International Enrollment Management Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF2562P Position Title Director of International Enrollment Management Position Type Professional/Salaried Department International Programs - Troy Division Student Affairs for Academic Affairs Campus Troy Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Director of International Enrollment Management position is responsible for recruitment of international students to Troy University; developing promotional materials for international programs and activities; coordinating recruiting for all Troy University locations including Troy University teaching sites abroad; working to diversify the international student population; analyze enrollment trends and set strategic recruiting plans; train and mentor staff to successfully recruit and admit international students; prepare weekly and monthly application and admissions reports; analyzing current agent partnerships; reporting on success; recommending continuation (or not) of agreements while also vetting potential new agent partners; maintaining correspondence with potential international students and agents; assisting agencies in placing students at Troy University; and supervising employees and student workers. Minimum Qualifications 1. Bachelor’s degree in a field related to International Relations, Hospitality, Travel, and/or Languages, or a related field 2. Proficiency in at least one second language 3. Knowledge of successful strategies and practices for marketing to, recruiting and serving university students 4. Strong communication skills and ability to communicate effectively with individuals whose native language may not be English Preferred Qualifications 1. Master Degree in a related field 2. Minimum of five years of work experience in international enrollment/education Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? Driving may be necessary but is not a primary responsibility Work Hours - Ability to work non-standard hours as needed, to include evenings and weekends - Ability to travel internationally in an official capacity for the university (must hold active passport and appropriate visas) List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position Travel internationally in other parts of the country. Does this position have supervisory responsibility? Yes Posting Date 07/22/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47932 Reference Letters Reference Letters Solicit References Through the System? No Last Day a Reference Provider Can Submit Reference Applicant Special Instructions Qualified applications will be made available to the department/committee for review immediately upon submission. We ask that you provide email addresses for your reference providers and please be certain that the email addresses you list are accurate. If you are selected as a candidate for consideration by the department/committee, an instructional email will be sent to your reference providers to ask that they submit a reference let