    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47778": {
      "title": "ALFA Eminent Scholar Graduate Fellow",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | ALFA Eminent Scholar Graduate Fellow Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions ALFA Eminent Scholar Graduate Fellow Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number ST1386P Position Title ALFA Eminent Scholar Graduate Fellow Position Type Student Department Biology - Troy Division College of Science and Engineering Campus Troy Work Status Student (SPT) Temporary Yes Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The ALFA Eminent Scholar Graduate Fellow is responsible for: - research activities such as collection, identification, photography, and database management for protozoans and microinvertebrates collected from the Gulf of Mexico and freshwater habitats; - protozoan isolation, meiofauna isolation (centrifugation), counting, histochemistry and microscopic preparation of samples as assigned; - laboratory maintenance and cleaning, inventory, assisting with scientific articles, writing drafts, running statistical tests., and creating maps using GIS . The applicant will be trained in these areas of responsibility. This position has a starting date of May 25th or August 1st, 2026 depending on the applicant’s availability. Minimum Qualifications 1. Bachelor’s degree in Biology or Environmental Science 2. Must be a Troy University graduate student enrolled in at least half time (unconditional admission) 3. Must be a thesis graduate student seeking a Master’s degree in Environmental Science or Biological Science in the ALFA scholar lab. 4. Must have and maintain a 3.0 GPA Please note: Student positions are FICA /Medicare exempt only if students are enrolled in classes in the semester work is performed. To qualify for the FICA /Medicare exemption, you must be enrolled on a half-time basis for the Fall, Spring, or Summer Preferred Qualifications 1. Good microscopy skills 2. Good computer skills Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? Driving may be necessary but is not a primary responsibility Work Hours Research activities not involving travel must be performed during business hours, 8AM-5PM, Mon-Fri. The workload will be 20 hours/week. List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position Ability to work in streams, rivers, and lakes and under environmental extremes. Ability to work on a research vessel at sea collecting samples. Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 07/06/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46267 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Do you currently work in another position for Troy University? No Yes - intend to keep other position Yes - intend to resign from other position * Will you hold a Bachelor’s degree in Biology or Environmental Science at the start of employment? Yes No * Will you be a Troy University graduate student seeking a Master's degree in Environmental Science or Biological Science at the start of employment? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Letter of Reference 1 Unofficial Transcript  1 Optional Documents Cover Letter List of References Letter of Reference 2 Unofficial Transcript  2 - Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. - Troy University is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. - Troy University participates in eVerify. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
