    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47508": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Research Assistant",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Undergraduate Research Assistant Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Undergraduate Research Assistant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number ST1365P Position Title Undergraduate Research Assistant Position Type Student Department Biology - Troy Division College of Science and Engineering Campus Troy Work Status Student (SPT) Temporary Yes Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Undergraduate Research Assistantin Biological and Environmental Sciences is responsible for conducting biotic surveys in south Alabama associated with the Blackwater Wetland Gradient study. This work includes but is not limited to: traveling to field locations, collecting data, completing data sheets, and participating in data entry and analysis. Minimum Qualifications 1) Must be a full-time Troy University undergraduate student 2) Must be comfortable working outdoors in strenuous conditions. 3) Must possess a valid driver’s license Please note: Student positions are FICA /Medicare exempt only if students are enrolled in classes in the semester work is performed. To qualify for the FICA /Medicare exemption, you must be enrolled on a half-time basis for the Fall, Spring, or Summer. Preferred Qualifications 1. Experience conducting fieldwork 2. Macroinvertebrate sampling and identification skills 3. Bird survey and identification skills. 4. Plant identification skills. Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? Driving may be necessary but is not a primary responsibility Work Hours To be determined Must be available for 10 hours per week throughout the semester List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position Ability to carry 10 pounds of weight Ability to navigate up and down stream banks Ability to conduct work outdoors in warm weather wearing PPE (waders, etc.) Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 09/24/2025 Closing Date 10/31/2025 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants TROY UNIVERSITY IS UNDER NO OBLIGATION TO MAINTAIN THIS POSITION IF FUNDING FROM EXTERNAL SOURCE IS REDUCED OR CEASED . Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/45564 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Do you currently work in another position for Troy University? No Yes - intend to keep other position Yes - intend to resign from other position * Are you a full-time Troy University undergraduate student? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume - Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. - Troy University is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. - Troy University participates in eVerify. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
