    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47872": {
      "title": "Donor Relations Specialist",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Donor Relations Specialist Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Donor Relations Specialist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF2557P Position Title Donor Relations Specialist Position Type Professional/Salaried Department Advancement Services Division Chancellor's Office Campus Troy Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Donor Relations Specialist position will serve as a member of the Office of Development and will play a key role in donor relations. The Donor Relations Specialist position will help implement a program with a goal of nurturing positive relationships with leadership donors. The program is composed primarily of donor relations, which includes cultivating and stewarding long-term relationships with leadership donors, as well as strategic and creative thinking around how to advance stewardship to a more sophisticated and personalized level. This individual will join a team that is committed to increasing philanthropic support of Troy University. Responsibilities/Duties -Manage reporting processes for endowed funds and current restricted gifts to ensure proper stewardship information is provided to donors to highlight the impact of their philanthropy on an annual basis -Maintain lists of donor recognition societies and execute recognition processes and coordinate with the Director of Annual Giving on society fundraising efforts. -Create recognition and feature stories to be displayed on the Development website. -Create customized donor stewardship plans on an annual basis for top donors in each of the frontline fundraising team’s portfolios -Manage all university-wide donor giving society courtesies, impact reporting, and programmatic experiences commensurate with level of giving. -Coordinate with each college-based Director of Development to support college-based giving societies -Manage donor relations touch points for special project and special giving day events. -Assist in analysis and evaluation of stewardship and donor relation programs; recommends new procedures to improve quality, effectiveness, and efficiency. -Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications 1. Bachelor’s degree in a related field 2. Minimum of three years of related work experience 3. Experience working with budgets 4. Excellent written and verbal communication skills 5. Strong organizational skills and an ability to prioritize 6. Ability to interact with a wide variety of constituents 7. Excellent computer skills Preferred Qualifications 1. Three to five years of experience with fundraising, donor relations or customer services fields Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? No Work Hours Monday thru Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position NA Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 07/16/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47861 Reference Letters Reference Letters Solicit References Through the System? No Last Day a Reference Provider Can Submit Reference Applicant Special Instructions Qualified applications will be made available to the department/c