      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Lecturer Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Lecturer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1081P Position Title Lecturer Position Type Faculty Department Department of C R I T - Global Division College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Campus Troy Online Faculty Rank If Faculty position 12 Month Is this position tenure track or non-tenure track? Non-Tenure Track Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location eTroy Job Summary The Lecturer in the Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training is responsible for teaching graduate-level counseling courses in a CACREP -accredited counselor education program. Responsibilities include course instruction, student advising and mentoring, clinical supervision of practicum and internship students, participation in curriculum development, support for student assessment and remediation processes, service to the department, and contribution to ongoing CACREP accreditation and program evaluation activities. In Class Teaching Percentage Online Teaching Percentage Minimum Qualifications 1. ‎Earned doctorate in Counselor Education from a CACREP -accredited program by the anticipated start date. 2. Professional identity as a counselor educator. 3. Experience in counseling, clinical supervision, or counselor education. 4. Ability to suppo