    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46797": {
      "title": "Workship",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Workship - Learning Center Peer Tutor - STEM Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Workship - Learning Center Peer Tutor - STEM Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number ST1128P Position Title Workship - Learning Center Peer Tutor - STEM Position Type Student Department Learning Center - Troy Division Academic Affairs Campus Troy Work Status Student (SPT) Temporary Yes Location Troy - T01 Job Summary This Workship position in Instructional Support Services is a student / peer position responsible for tutoring Troy Campus students and helping present information related to Learning Center services and the tutor’s subject concentration(s). Applicants with accounting, finance, economics or computer science minors may be considered, if they also have a Math or Science major. This is not a Graduate Assistantship position nor does it provide tuition assistance. Minimum Qualifications 1. Must be a current Troy University student enrolled at least half-time. 2. Must hold a 3.0 GPA or higher 3. Must be a Math or Science major 4. Must be able to use Microsoft Teams 5. Must work cooperatively with others Please note: Student positions are FICA /Medicare exempt only if students are enrolled in classes in the semester work is performed. To qualify for the FICA /Medicare exemption, you must be enrolled on a half-time basis for the Fall, Spring, or Summer. Preferred Qualifications 1. Faculty/Staff referral 2. Tutoring experience 3. Three semesters prior to graduation 4. Summer work availability preferred but not required Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? No Work Hours 10 to 15 hours per week – hours will vary List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 03/04/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants All applicants should clarify in their resumes any subject concentration areas in which they can effectively tutor and have tutoring experience. Tutors should also clearly indicate anticipated graduation dates and degree programs in their resumes. Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/39400 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Are you a current Troy University student enrolled at least half-time, or will you be enrolled at least half-time by the start of employment? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Unofficial Transcript  1 Optional Documents - Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. - Troy University is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. - Troy University participates in eVerify. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
