    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47702": {
      "title": "AMSTI Math/Science Specialist",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | AMSTI Math/Science Specialist Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions AMSTI Math/Science Specialist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF2547P Position Title AMSTI Math/Science Specialist Position Type Professional/Salaried Department AMSTI - Troy Division College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Campus Troy Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The AMSTI Math/Science Specialist position is responsible for providing frequent and on-going professional learning and on-site assistance to K-12 teachers and administrators in Region 11; spending the majority of work time regulated to on-site support, including travel to and from the site; assisting with preparation for professional learning opportunities; assisting schools in effectively using learning teams and common planning time to improve math and science instruction; providing training and guidance to teachers; participation in professional development activities and staff meetings as required by ALSDE ; and performing other duties assigned by the AMSTI site director or AMSTI state director. Minimum Qualifications 1. Bachelor’s degree in a Math and/or Science related field 2. Alabama teaching certification 3. Teaching experience in the associated subject and grade band 4. Valid driver’s license Preferred Quali