n an as-needed basis. In Class Teaching Percentage Online Teaching Percentage Minimum Qualifications 1. An earned graduate degree in nursing. 2. An active, unencumbered Alabama registered nurse license, or a multistate registered nurse license issued by a party state. 3. Academic and experiential qualifications to teach in the area assigned. 4. A minimum of at least two years of employment as a registered nurse. Preferred Qualifications 1. Doctoral degree in nursing of related field. 2. National certification. 3. Previous teaching experience in a nursing program. Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? No Work Hours To be determined List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position NA Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 01/25/2017 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Adjunct postings are intended to serve as a means of accumulating an applicant pool for prospective Adjunct Instructors. Applications will be reviewed as positions become available. Applications may remain active for an extended period of time as the department pulls applicants from the pool to serve in positions on an as-needed basis. Academic Term Position Will Begin As needed Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/15820 Reference Letters Reference Letters Last Day a Reference Provider Can Submit Reference Applicant Special Instructions Qualified applications will be made available to the department/committee for review immediately upon submission. We ask that you provide email addresses for your reference providers and please be certain that the email addresses you list are accurate. If you are selected as a candidate for consideration by the department/committee, an instructional email will be sent to your reference providers to ask that they submit a reference letter on your behalf via a link t