    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48402": {
      "title": "Senior Educational Technology Administrator",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Senior Educational Technology Administrator Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Senior Educational Technology Administrator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF2593P Position Title Senior Educational Technology Administrator Position Type Professional/Salaried Department Information Technology - Troy Division Finance and Administration Campus Troy Online Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Senior Educational Technology Administrator serves as an administrator for the University’s Canvas Learning Management System ( LMS ), ensuring its reliability, security, availability, and optimal performance to support teaching and learning. This position provides advanced technical support by troubleshooting and resolving complex Canvas-related issues for faculty, staff, students, and administrators while maintaining a high level of customer service in a fast-paced support environment. Manages and resolves support requests through the TeamDynamix ticketing system, responds to escalated support cases referred by Instructure Support, including Canvas chat sessions and institutional support tickets requiring administrative intervention, and performs remote troubleshooting sessions using approved remote support software. This position is responsible for creating Canvas organizations used for university communications, faculty development, student engagement, training initiatives, and other institutional purposes. The Senior Administrator also develops, updates, and maintains online student training courses designed to orient first-time Canvas users and promote successful navigation and utilization of the University’s learning management system. The Senior Systems Administrator maintains, and supports educational technology applications that integrate with Canvas, including Turnitin Plagiarism Detection, Respondus LockDown Browser and Monitor, Respondus 4.0 Test Bank, NetTutor Online Tutoring, Microsoft Teams, Camtasia, Watermarks’ Student Learning and Licensure and other Learning Tools Interoperability ( LTI ) applications and third-party instructional technologies, such as- Pearson and McGraw-Hill. The position develops and maintains comprehensive technical documentation, standard operating procedures, user guides, and TeamDynamix Knowledge Base articles to support self-service resources and improve the overall user experience. This position requires evening and weekend work to provide technical support to end users, perform system maintenance, software upgrades, and emergency troubleshooting. Minimum Qualifications 1. Bachelor’s degree in a related field OR Minimum of five years of experience working within an educational technology technical support area 2. Strong troubleshooting and analytical skills with the ability to diagnose and resolve complex technical issues. 3. Ability to manage multiple tasks and prioritize those tasks effectively 4. Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to create clear technical documentation and knowledge base articles. 5. Excellent computer skills 6. Ability to work with diverse individuals of various backgrounds Preferred Qualifications 1. Master’s degree preferred 2. Knowledge of higher education instructional technologies, accessibility standards, and online learning environments 3. Skill in installation, trouble-shooting and maintenance of technology hardware and software systems related to learning management systems ( LMS ) Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? No Work Hours Monday-Friday, 8-5 Afternoons and weekends as needed. List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position NA Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 09/03/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48400 Reference Letters Reference Letters Solicit References Through the System? No Last Day a Reference Provider Can Submit Reference Applicant Special Instructions Qualified applications will be made available to the department/committee for review immediately upon submission. We ask that you provide email addresses for your reference providers and please be certain that the email addresses you list are accurate. If you are selected as a candidate for consideration by the department/committee, an instructional email will be sent to your reference providers to ask that they submit a reference letter on your behalf via a link to our reference portal. Separate reference letters will be requested for each position to which you apply (if applicable), so your reference providers will be contacted separately for each application on which you list them. Reference letters will not be copied from one application to another. You can assure your reference providers that our system is secure and that all letters are confidential. If your reference providers have trouble using the reference portal, please advise them to contact jobs@troy.edu. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Regarding your current employment status, please select one of the following: Not a current Troy University employee Current part-time Troy employee (including adjunct faculty) Current full-time Troy employee - initial appraisal period complete Current full-time Troy employee - still within initial appraisal period (six months for new employees and three months for promoted employees) * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree in a related field, OR a minimum of five years of experience working within an educational technology technical support area? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Unofficial Transcript  1 - Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. - Troy University is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. - Troy University participates in eVerify. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
