s or a related field upon completion of the master’s program. 5. Professional Potential : Demonstrated potential through letters of recommendation, a statement of purpose, or previous research experience. Preferred Qualifications 1. Strong communication skills showing both oral and written proficiency 2. Strong quantitative skills Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? Driving may be necessary but is not a primary responsibility Work Hours 20 hours per week List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position This position involves potential exposure to hazardous chemicals, biological agents, and sharp instruments in the lab, as well as environmental risks such as extreme weather and uneven terrain during fieldwork. Physical demands include extended periods of standing, repetitive motions, lifting up to 25 pounds, and travel to field sites. Proper safety training, equipment, and protocols will be provided to mitigate these risks. Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 06/03/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47543 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a Bachelor's degree in Biological Sciences or a related field? Yes No * Are you a current Troy University graduate student? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List 