      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Global Leadership Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Adjunct Faculty - Global Leadership Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F0697P Position Title Adjunct Faculty - Global Leadership Position Type Adjunct Faculty Department Department of Leadership, Development and Professional Studies - Global Campus Division College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Campus Troy Faculty Rank Adjunct Faculty If Faculty position Adjunct Is this position tenure track or non-tenure track? Non-Tenure Track Work Status Adjunct (APT) Temporary Yes Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Adjunct Faculty position for Global Leadership is responsible for teaching doctoral level courses ranging from content (e.g., global leadership and organizational management) to research methods (e.g., introduction to research, research design). Courses will be assigned based on the specific credentials that are within the faculty member’s educational coursework and professional background.  This position is also responsible for developing curriculum, course materials, video lectures, labs, and presentations as assigned; and participating in program and course level learning assessments.  This position may be expected to serve on dissertation committees, as assigned by the program director. Other responsibilities: - Preparation of interactive presentations for quality face-to-face and online teaching - Respond to student inquiries in a timely manner - Provision of substantive and ongoing feedback to students - Maintenance and enhancement of the quality of teaching in the program - Attendance at adjunct faculty meetings In Class Teaching Percentage Online Teaching Percentage Minimum Qualifications 1. Doctorate degree from an accredited university in leadership, global leadership, or one of the following specialization content areas: Instructional Leadership and Administration (K-12), Public Administration, Organizational Leadership, Strategic Communication, Higher Education 2. Minimum of five years of teaching experience at a graduate (preferably doctoral) level 3. Evidence of online teaching experience 4. Record of active research and publications in peer-reviewed academic journals 5. Understanding and commitment to cultural proficiency, diversity, equity, and social justice 6. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Preferred Qualifications 1. Experience in guiding doctoral research 2. Record of international experience and/or unique understanding and familiarity with specific nations or cultures 3. Experience teaching working professionals who pursue graduate degrees by attending classes in evenings, on weekends, and in both face-to-face and hybrid learning environments Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? Driving may be necessary but is not a primary responsibility Work Hours To be determined by departmental needs List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position NA Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 10/21/2019 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Academic Term Position Will Begin Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/26729 Reference Letters Reference Lette