    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47873": {
      "title": "Donor Stewardship Specialist",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Donor Stewardship Specialist Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Donor Stewardship Specialist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF2558P Position Title Donor Stewardship Specialist Position Type Professional/Salaried Department Advancement Services Division Chancellor's Office Campus Troy Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Donor Stewardship Specialist will serve as a member of the Office of Development team and will play a key role in donor stewardship and fund management. The Donor Stewardship Specialist will work closely with the Development team and University colleagues to organize and review data to facilitate decision-making in support of engagement and stewardship strategies. This individual will identify and implement best practices to ensure that agreements and reporting are kept in University standards and meet donor expectations. Duties and Responsibilities: Provide Annual Statements to donors Deliver Monthly Fund Reports to appropriate colleges/departments Work on gift agreements/scholarship agreements Implement new donor recognition letters at all levels Ensure all contributions are receipted in a timely manner Produce and mail all monthly pledge reminders and recurring credit card donor reminders Collaborate with Donor Relations on endowment reports, impact reports, donor/campus stories, etc. Gather all necessary data requested for those by connecting with Foundation Accounting, appropriate Colleges/Departments, Raiser’s Edge system, etc. Quarterly review of all Foundation fund administration. Work with Development Officers and other Fund Administrators on fund purpose and utilization. Assist in the process of awarding Foundation Scholarships each academic year. Work with all awarding parties and Academic Works manager in notification of awarding amount memos as well as what scholarship have not been awarded and need awarding throughout the academic year. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a related field Minimum of two years of related work experience Excellent written and verbal communication skills Strong organizational skills and an ability to prioritize Ability to interact with a wide variety of constituents Excellent computer skills Preferred Qualifications 1. Two to five years of experience in fundraising, donor stewardship or customer services fields Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? No Work Hours Monday-Friday 8am-5pm List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position NA Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 07/16/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47860 Reference Letters Reference Letters Solicit References Through the System? No Last Day a Reference Provider Can Submit Reference Applicant Special Instructions Qualified applications will be made available to the department/committee for review immediately upon submission. We ask that you provide email addresses for your reference providers and please be certain that the email addresses you list are accurate. If you are selected as a candidate for consideration by the department/c