    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48010": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Assistant/Associate Professor Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Assistant/Associate Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1080P Position Title Assistant/Associate Professor Position Type Faculty Department Department of C R I T - Troy Division College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Campus Troy Faculty Rank If Faculty position 12 Month Is this position tenure track or non-tenure track? Tenure Track Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training position in the College of Education is an on-ground faculty appointment located at the Troy, Alabama campus. The position is primarily responsible for teaching specialized graduate courses in clinical mental health counseling and other counseling specialties; maintaining an active program of scholarship, research, and professional contribution; advising and mentoring graduate students; supervising practicum and internship students; supporting CACREP accreditation and program assessment activities; and providing service to the department, college, university, profession, and community. In Class Teaching Percentage Online Teaching Percentage Minimum Qualifications 1. Earned doctorate in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP -accredited program by the date of appointment. 2. Professional identity as a counselor demonstrated through academic preparation, professional experience, licensure, and active engagement in the counseling profession. 3. Eligibility for licensure as a Professional Counselor in Alabama (e.g., LPC or equivalent). 4. Academic preparation and/or professional experience in Clinical Mental Health Counseling, School Counseling, Rehabilitation Counseling, or another CACREP -recognized specialty area. 5. Demonstrated potential for excellence in graduate teaching, student mentoring, and supervision. 6. Demonstrated potential for scholarly productivity consistent with expectations for tenure and promotion. 7. Ability to teach in both face-to-face and online learning environments. 8. Excellent written, oral, interpersonal, and organizational communication skills. Preferred Qualifications 1. Current unrestricted Professional Counselor licensure ( LPC or equivalent). 2. Experience teaching in a CACREP -accredited counselor education program. 3. Experience supervising practicum and internship students consistent with CACREP standards. 4. Record of scholarly activity, including peer-reviewed publications, conference presentations, externally funded grants, or other evidence of an active research agenda. 5. Experience with CACREP accreditation, program evaluation, student learning assessment, or continuous quality improvement processes. 6. Experience developing and delivering high-quality online or hybrid graduate instruction. 7. Experience advising and mentoring graduate students. 8. Evidence of interdisciplinary collaboration, leadership, and professional service at the state, regional, or national level. 9. Demonstrated commitment to working effectively with students from diverse backgrounds and fostering an inclusive learning environment. 10. Expertise in one or more areas that complement departmental needs, such as: Clinical Mental Health Counseling School Counseling Rehabilitation Counseling Addictions Counseling Counselor Supervision Assessment and Diagnosis Crisis and Trauma Child and Adolescent Counseling Integrated Behavioral Health Military or Rural Mental Health Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? Driving may be necessary but is not a primary responsibility Work Hours As needed based on course schedule & departmental needs. List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position NA Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 07/28/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Academic Term Position Will Begin Fall 2026 Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47997 Reference Letters Reference Letters Last Day a Reference Provider Can Submit Reference Applicant Special Instructions Qualified applications will be made available to the department/committee for review immediately upon submission. We ask that you provide email addresses for your reference providers and please be certain that the email addresses you list are accurate. If you are selected as a candidate for consideration by the department/committee, an instructional email will be sent to your reference providers to ask that they submit a reference letter on your behalf via a link to our reference portal. Separate reference letters will be requested for each position to which you apply (if applicable), so your reference providers will be contacted separately for each application on which you list them. Reference letters will not be copied from one application to another. You can assure your reference providers that our system is secure and that all letters are confidential. If your reference providers have trouble using the reference portal, please advise them to contact jobs@troy.edu. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). *