      "title": "Workship",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Workship Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Workship Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number ST1454P Position Title Workship Position Type Student Department Assessment & Technology - Troy Division College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Campus Troy Work Status Student (SPT) Temporary Yes Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Workship position in Assessment & Technology is responsible for assisting the Technology Coordinator with the maintenance of computer labs and classroom technology in Hawkins Hall, including cleaning two computer labs and assisting with updating broken equipment for upgraded versions in 16 classrooms; and maintaining stock inventory of all needed equipment. Minimum Qualifications 1. Must be a current Troy University student 2. Knowledge of computer hardware and peripherals such as ELMO document cameras, and desktop/laptops in the PC format rather than MAC 3. Ability to connect USB , HDMI , and VGA cables and exhibit good cable management practices Please note: Student positions are FICA /Medicare tax exempt only if students are enrolled in classes in the semester work is performed. To qualify for the FICA /Medicare tax exemption, you must be enrolled on a half-time basis for the Fall, Spring, and/or Summer. Preferred Qualifications 1. Currently enrolled in an IT or computer science program 2. Experience with audio/visual equipment 3. Ability to work during the summer 4. Proficient in assembling carts, tables, etc. Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? Driving may be necessary but is not a primary responsibility Work Hours Based on student class schedule List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position Ability to lift and/or move up to 40 pounds Ability to climb ladders and work above the head with ease Ability to bend and work in low cramped areas Ability to upgrade equipment by picking up and installing speakers, webcams, projectors, etc. Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 07/21/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47895 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Do you currently work in another position for Troy University? No Yes - if hired for this position, intend to resign from other position Yes - if hired for this position, intend to keep other position * Are you a current Troy University student? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Unofficial Transcript  1 Unofficial Transcript  2 Other Document - Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. - Troy University is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. - Troy University participates in eVerify. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
