    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48328": {
      "title": "Director, Student Services Business Office",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Director, Student Services Business Office Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Director, Student Services Business Office Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF2585P Position Title Director, Student Services Business Office Position Type Professional/Salaried Department Controller's Office - Troy Division Finance and Administration Campus Troy Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Director position in the Student Services Business Office (under the supervision of the Controller’s Office) assists the Student Services Department with management and oversight of fiscal operations to include tax compliance, budgeting services, payment services, monitoring of internal controls, and financial reporting to the Controller’s Office. Essential Functions: - Advises, establishes, maintains, and monitors a strong system of financial and internal controls for the Student Services Department in coordination with the Dean of Student Services. - Builds and maintains financial templates and reports as needed in the current financial reporting software. Prepares financial reports, department allocation reports, inventory reports or other specialized reports on a regular or ad hoc basis. - Assists in the development of the annual budget as well as detailed monthly analysis of Student Services revenue and spend history. Reviews, analyzes, approves, and prepares budget transfers and other accounting allocations. - Assists the Controller’s Office and Foundation Accounting with the tracking, reporting, and compliance of all Student Services Department transactions. Prepares and reviews expense vouchers, invoices, purchase requisitions or other transactions for one or more departments, in compliance with approved budgets, University and/or Foundation policy and with appropriate delegation of tasks to the Student Services Staff Accountant. - Assists with the fiscal year-end process and preparation of the annual financial report to include reconciliation and review of financial accounts or processes as needed throughout the year. - Assist the Controller’s Office as needed and assume additional duties and responsibilities as assigned, including providing support for accounting, financial reporting, and other operational functions. Minimum Qualifications 1. Bachelor’s degree in Accounting from an accredited institution. 2. Minimum of five years of accounting, budget and/or financial management experience at progressively responsible levels. Preferred Qualifications 1. Master’s degree in Accounting from an accredited institution 2. Experience at an institution of higher education in budgeting or accounting services functions Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? Driving may be necessary but is not a primary responsibility Work Hours Monday – Friday 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibility? Yes Posting Date 08/26/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48326 Reference Letters Reference Letters Solicit References Through the System? No Last Day a Re