      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Lecturer Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Lecturer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1082P Position Title Lecturer Position Type Faculty Department Department of C R I T - Global Division College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Campus Troy Online Faculty Rank If Faculty position 12 Month Is this position tenure track or non-tenure track? Non-Tenure Track Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location eTroy Job Summary The Lecturer in the Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training is responsible for teaching graduate-level counseling courses in a CACREP -accredited counselor education program. Responsibilities include course instruction, student advising and mentoring, clinical supervision of practicum and internship students, participation in curriculum development, support for student assessment and remediation processes, service to the department, and contribution to ongoing CACREP accreditation and program evaluation activities. In Class Teaching Percentage Online Teaching Percentage Minimum Qualifications 1. ‎Earned doctorate in Counselor Education from a CACREP -accredited program by the anticipated start date. 2. Professional identity as a counselor educator. 3. Experience in counseling, clinical supervision, or counselor education. 4. Ability to support CACREP accreditation expectations, including instruction, student assessment, and clinical training. 5. Strong written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications 1. Licensed or license-eligible as a Professional Counselor in the State of Alabama. 2. Experience teaching graduate counseling courses. 3. Experience supervising practicum and internship students. 4. Experience with CACREP standards, assessment, remediation, or program evaluation. 5. Experience advising and mentoring graduate students. 6. Professional experience in clinical mental health counseling, school counseling, rehabilitation counseling, or a related counseling specialty. Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? Driving may be necessary but is not a primary responsibility Work Hours Based on teaching schedule and departmental needs List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position NA Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 07/28/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Academic Term Position Will Begin Fall 2026 Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47999 Reference Letters Reference Letters Last Day a Reference Provider Can Submit Reference Applicant Special Instructions Qualified applications will be made available to the department/committee for review immediately upon submission. We ask that you provide email addresses for your reference providers and please be certain that the email addresses you list are accurate. If you are selected as a candidate for consideration by the department/committee, an instructional email will be sent to your reference providers to ask that they submit a reference letter on your behalf via a link to our reference portal. Separate reference letters will be requested for each position to which you apply (if applicable), so your referen