      "title": "Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor - Biology Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Adjunct Instructor - Biology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F0476P Position Title Adjunct Instructor - Biology Position Type Adjunct Faculty Department Biology Division College of Science and Engineering Campus All Campuses Faculty Rank Adjunct Faculty If Faculty position Adjunct Is this position tenure track or non-tenure track? Non-Tenure Track Work Status Adjunct (APT) Temporary Yes Location All Locations Job Summary Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct instructors are expected to be available for reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. In Class Teaching Percentage Online Teaching Percentage Minimum Qualifications 1. Bachelor’s degree in Biological or Environmental Science 2. 18 hours of graduate level coursework in Biological or Environmental Science 3. Experience in the use of educational technology and/or distance learning Preferred Qualifications Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? No Work Hours To be determined List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position NA Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 01/25/2017 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Adjunct postings are intended to serve as a means of accumulating an applicant pool for prospective Adjunct Instructors. Applications will be reviewed as positions become available. Applications may remain active for an extended period of time as the department pulls applicants from the pool to serve in positions on an as-needed basis. Academic Term Position Will Begin As needed Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/15722 Reference Letters Reference Letters Last Day a Reference Provider Can Submit Reference Applicant Special Instructions Qualified applications will be made available to the department/committee for review immediately upon submission. We ask that you provide email addresses for your reference providers and please be certain that the email addresses you list are accurate. If you are selected as a candidate for consideration by the department/committee, an instructional email will be sent to your reference providers to ask that they submit a reference letter on your behalf via a link to our reference portal. Separate reference letters will be requested for each position to which you apply (if applicable), so your reference providers will be contacted separately for each application on which you list them. Reference letters will not be copied from one application to another. You can assure your reference providers that our system is secure and that all letters are confidential. If your reference providers have trouble using the reference portal, please advise them to contact jobs@troy.edu. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Regarding your current employment status, please select one of the following: Not a current Troy University employee Current part-time Troy employee (including adjunct faculty) Current full-time Troy employee - initial appraisal period complete Current full-time Troy employee - still within initial appraisal period (six months for new employees and three months for promoted employees) * Please indicate the location(s) at which you are willing and able to work: \r\nOnline; \r\nTroy Campus (AL); \r\nMontgomery Campus (AL); \r\nDothan Campus (AL); \r\nPhenix City Campus (AL); \r\nFort Walton Beach, FL; \r\nTyndall AFB, FL; \r\nPanama City, FL; \r\nPensacola, FL; \r\nOrlando, FL; \r\nTampa, FL; \r\nAlbany, GA; \r\nAtlanta, GA; \r\nAugusta/Fort Gordon, GA; \r\nBrunswick, GA; \r\nCovington, GA; \r\nColumbus/Fort Benning, GA; \r\nSavannah, GA; \r\nFayetteville, NC; \r\nSumter, SC; \r\nClarksville, TN; \r\nSan Antonio, TX; \r\nHampton Roads, VA; \r\nKadena AFB, Japan; \r\nMisawa AFB, Japan; \r\nOsan AFB, Korea; \r\nYongsan AFB, Korea; and/or \r\nCamp Humphreys, Korea (Open Ended Question) * Please indicate the highest level degree you have received in the discipline of the posting or a related discipline: Bachelor's degree; Master's degree; PhD; or Other (Open Ended Question) * Please list the specific discipline of the degree you received and/or the area of specialization: (Open Ended Question) * Please list any related certifications and/or licenses you hold: (Open Ended Question) * Please describe any teaching experience you may have: (Open Ended Question) * Please describe any related professional experience you may have: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Unofficial Transcript  1 Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Unofficial Transcript  2 - Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. - Troy University is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. - Troy University participates in eVerify. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46798": {
      "title": "Workship",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Workship - Writing Center Tutor Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Workship - Writing Center Tutor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number ST1221P Position Title Workship - Writing Center Tutor Position Type Student Department Learning Center - Troy Division Academic Affairs Campus Troy Work Status Student (SPT) Temporary Yes Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Workship – Writing Center Tutor position in Instructional Support Services is responsible for tutoring Troy University students in writing improvement. Minimum Qualifications 1. Must be a current Troy University student enrolled at least half-time. 2. GPA of 3.0 or higher 3. Completion of English 1101/1102 or 1103/1104, earning at least a B in each course 4. One recommendation from English faculty 5. Good interpersonal communication skills 6. Commitment to the goals and objectives of the Writing Center 7. Excellent writing skills as evidenced in application essay 8. Willingness to help actively promote Learning Center services, events, and activities. Please note: Student positions are FICA /Medicare exempt only if students are enrolled in classes in the semester work is performed. To qualify for the FICA /Medicare exemption, you must be enrolled on a half-time basis for the Fall, Spring, or Summer. Preferred Qualifications 1. Knowledge of APA Style, MLA Style, and/or other writing formats to help students avoid plagiarism issues 2. Online and in-person tutoring experience Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? No Work Hours Varies according to Writing Center needs and student’s schedule List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position NA Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 03/04/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/41749 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Are you a current Troy University student enrolled at least half-time, or will you be enrolled at least half-time by the start of employment? Yes No * Do you have a GPA of at least 3.0? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Reference 1 Unofficial Transcript  1 Optional Documents List of References Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Unofficial Transcript  2 Unofficial Transcript 3 - Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. - Troy University is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. - Troy University participates in eVerify. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47751": {
      "title": "Graduate Administrative Assistant-Music Education",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Graduate Administrative Assistant-Music Education Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Graduate Administrative Assistant-Music Education Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number ST1452P Position Title Graduate Administrative Assistant-Music Education Position Type Student Department Music - Troy Division College of Arts and Humanities Campus Troy Work Status Student (SPT) Temporary Yes Location Troy - T01 Job Summary This position will work closely with the Coordinator of Music Education and Director of the School of Music. The responsibilities include: 1. Serve as a liaison between the School of Music and the Department of Teacher Education to coordinate clinical field placements for undergraduate Music Education students. 2. Support the maintenance of a database containing clinical field placement information. 3. Organize and update Music Education classroom inventory using a shared Excel spreadsheet. 4. Assist in maintaining a recruitment database for prospective Music Education students (choral graduate assistants will coordinate with choral faculty on a separate choral database, while band graduate assistants will work with band faculty to manage a database for prospective band students). 5. Contribute to the planning and coordination of Music Education Day. 6. Assist with all School of Music recruitment events. 7. Collaborate with music faculty and graduate assistants (Choral, Band, and Music Industry) to maintain a comprehensive School of Music recruitment database, including establishing consistent communication with prospective students and high school music teachers. 8. Support the management of the School of Music’s social media platforms. Minimum Qualifications 1. Bachelor’s degree in Music Education, Music, or music related field. Preferred Qualifications Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? No Work Hours 20 hours per week List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position None Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 06/22/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47668 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Do you currently work in another position for Troy University? No Yes - intend to keep other position Yes - intend to resign from other position * Are you a current Troy University graduate student? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Unofficial Transcript  1 Optional Documents - Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. - Troy University is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. - Troy University participates in eVerify. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
